nomy changed adult content more than any technology did. Performers can now run their own businesses and keep most of the revenue. Leak sites exist to break that, and understanding the trade clarifies why direct support matters.</p></div>\n<nav class=\"toc\" aria-label=\"Table of contents\"><p class=\"toc-h\">Contents</p><ul><li><a href=\"#how-the-direct-model-works-1\">How the direct model works</a></li><li><a href=\"#what-a-leak-site-actually-does-2\">What a leak site actually does</a></li><li><a href=\"#the-practical-case-not-just-the-moral-one-3\">The practical case, not just the moral one</a></li><li><a href=\"#where-we-point-4\">Where we point</a></li><li><a href=\"#more-creators-guides-5\">More Creators guides</a></li></ul></nav>\n<div class=\"article-meta\"><span>Dark-Ero editorial</span><span>2026-09-30</span></div>\n<article class=\"prose\">\n    <p style=\"font-size:18px;color:var(--text)\">The free version of paid content has a price. It is just paid by someone else.</p>\n    <p>The creator economy changed adult content more than any technology did. Performers can now run their own businesses and keep most of the revenue. Leak sites exist to break that, and understanding the trade clarifies why direct support matters.</p><h2 id=\"how-the-direct-model-works-1\">How the direct model works</h2><p>On subscription platforms, a viewer pays a creator, the platform takes a cut, and the creator keeps the rest. It is the first model in the industry's history where the person on camera controls the business. That is worth protecting.</p><h2 id=\"what-a-leak-site-actually-does-2\">What a leak site actually does</h2><p>A leak site takes that paid content and gives it away to draw traffic it can monetise with advertising. The creator earns nothing, the leak site earns everything, and the viewer funds a stranger's ad revenue while believing they got something for free.</p><div class=\"callout safe\"><p>Many creators offer free tiers, previews and public accounts precisely so people can sample their work honestly. That is the free access worth using — given, not taken.</p></div><h2 id=\"the-practical-case-not-just-the-moral-one-3\">The practical case, not just the moral one</h2><p>Leak sites are also among the most malware-dense pages on the web, precisely because they attract people looking for something for nothing. The free content often comes bundled with a cost you didn't agree to. Direct support is safer as well as fairer.</p><h2 id=\"where-we-point-4\">Where we point</h2><p>Our Creators section links only to official, creator-controlled pages. It is a smaller list than a leak aggregator, and every entry on it sends your attention to the person who earned it.</p>\n    <div class=\"callout safe\"><p>Browsing this topic? See the <a href=\"/category/sell-feet-pics/\">Creators</a> section of the directory for hand-checked sites.</p></div>\n    <hr class=\"divider\" style=\"margin:34px 0\">\n    <p style=\"font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)\">This guide is general information, not legal or security advice. Laws on adult content vary by country — check what applies where you live.</p>\n  </article>\n  <div style=\"display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:30px 0\"><a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/blog/vr-adult-content-headset-compatibility-explained-plainly/\">← VR adult content: headset compatib…</a><a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/blog/browser-hygiene-for-private-adult-browsing/\">Browser hygiene for private adult … →</a></div>\n  <section class=\"section\" style=\"padding-top:0\">\n    <div class=\"section-head\"><h2 id=\"more-creators-guides-5\">More Creators guides</h2><a href=\"/blog/topic/creators/\">All →</a></div>\n    <div class=\"post-list\"><article class=\"post-card\">\n      <div class=\"tagline\"><a href=\"/blog/topic/safety/\" style=\"color:inherit\">Safety</a></div>\n      <h3><a href=\"/blog/how-to-tell-a-real-adult-site-from-a-malware-trap/\">How to tell a real adult site from a malware trap</a></h3>\n      <p>The five signals that separate a legitimate platform from a page that just wants your browser.</p>\n      <a class=\"more\" href=\"/blog/how-to-tell-a-real-adult-site-from-a-malware-trap/\">Read guide →</a>\n    </article><article class=\"post-card\">\n      <div class=\"tagline\"><a href=\"/blog/topic/guides/\" style=\"color:inherit\">Guides</a></div>\n      <h3><a href=\"/blog/free-versus-premium-what-you-are-actually-paying-for/\">Free versus premium: what you are actually paying for</a></h3>\n      <p>The real trade is not price against no-price. It is your attention against your money.</p>\n      <a class=\"more\" href=\"/blog/free-versus-premium-what-you-are-actually-paying-for/\">Read guide →</a>\n    </article><article class=\"post-card\">\n      <div class=\"tagline\"><a href=\"/blog/topic/safety/\" style=\"color:inherit\">Safety</a></div>\n      <h3><a href=\"/blog/why-free-onlyfans-links-are-almost-always-a-scam/\">Why &#x27;free OnlyFans&#x27; links are almost always a scam</a></h3>\n      <p>The search term is popular. The destinations behind it are a minefield of malware, fraud and stolen content.</p>\n      <a class=\"more\" href=\"/blog/why-free-onlyfans-links-are-almost-always-a-scam/\">Read guide →</a>\n    </article></div>\n  </section>\n</article></main>\n<footer class=\"site-foot de-foot\">\n  <div class=\"de-foot-band\"><div class=\"container\">\n    <div class=\"de-foot-top\">\n      <a class=\"brand\" href=\"/\"><img class=\"brand-logo\" src=\"/assets/logo.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\"><span class=\"wordmark\"><b>Dark</b><span class=\"ero\">-Ero</span></span></a>\n      <p>An independent adult-site directory. Listings go straight to the site. Scores appear only after a real review.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"de-foot-icons\">\n      <a href=\"/contact/\" aria-label=\"Contact\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"5\" width=\"18\" 